# shape_constraint_reject.tkr — the §9.2b shape-constraint REJECT channel: five constraint violations,
# one per namespace under src/, reported by a single failing build. Each row pins a refusal the solver
# must keep making. `notnull_in_or_rejected` is the GRAMMAR refusal (rejected at parse time, before any
# instantiation exists); the other four are SOLVER refusals raised where the generic is instantiated.
# `service_transient_where_singleton_rejected` is the §9.2b honest-lifetime ruling itself: a transport
# of the wrong lifetime FAILS COMPILATION rather than being silently redirected to singleton — the
# whole reason the lifetime rides in the constraint. The ACCEPT twin is
# `examples/regressions/shape_constraint`.

Feature: shape_constraint_reject — §9.2b rejects notnull-in-`|`, a wrong service lifetime, a wrong form, a wrong concrete type, and an unsatisfied disjunction

  Scenario: notnull_in_or_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "`notnull` may not be a `|` alternative — it is a non-null modifier, use it with `&` (e.g. `class & notnull`) (§9.2b)"

  Scenario: service_transient_where_singleton_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "type parameter 'T' does not satisfy its constraint at this instantiation"

  Scenario: class_form_on_struct_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "type parameter 'T' does not satisfy its constraint at this instantiation"

  Scenario: concrete_type_mismatch_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "type parameter 'T' does not satisfy its constraint at this instantiation"

  Scenario: disjunction_no_alt_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "type parameter 'T' does not satisfy its constraint at this instantiation"
